{
  "agent": {
    "alerts_given": "- HighRequestErrorRate (frontend)\n- HighRequestErrorRate (frontend-proxy)\n- HighRequestLatency (accounting)",
    "commands": [
      "kubectl -n otel-demo get pods -o wide; kubectl -n otel-demo get events --sort-by=.lastTimestamp | tail -20",
      "cd /tmp; for d in frontend frontend-proxy accounting checkout; do echo \"== $d\"; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/$d --tail=15 2>&1 | cut -c1-300; done; kubectl -n otel-demo get cm -o name",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n otel-demo get cm flagd-config -o yaml | grep -B3 -A8 -E '\"defaultVariant\": \"(on|[^o])' | head -150",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/frontend --tail=300 | grep -v '\"http.response.status_code\":200' | cut -c1-400 | tail -15",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n otel-demo get cm flagd-config -o yaml | grep -E 'defaultVariant|^    \"|^      \"[a-zA-Z]+\": \\{' | head -60; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/frontend-proxy --tail=2000 | grep -E '\" (5[0-9][0-9]) ' | tail -5; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/frontend --tail=3000 | grep -E '\"level\":(50|40)' | cut -c1-500 | tail -5",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n otel-demo get svc | grep 10.96.129.134; kubectl -n otel-demo get endpoints | head -40; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/frontend --since=60s | grep -c '\"level\":50'; kubectl -n otel-demo top pod 2>&1 | head -30",
      "cd /tmp; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/frontend-proxy --since=90s | grep -cE ' 5[0-9][0-9] '; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/frontend-proxy --since=90s | tail -3 | cut -c1-250; kubectl -n otel-demo logs deploy/accounting --since=60s | grep -ciE 'error|exception|warn'"
    ],
    "exit_code": 0,
    "image": "sremut-agent:k8s-1.37",
    "is_error": false,
    "limit_reached": false,
    "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
    "seconds": 24,
    "summary": "I made no changes. The incident looks like a transient startup problem that had already cleared by the time I looked.\n\n- **State of the cluster:** All pods in `otel-demo` are Running with 0 restarts. All pods were about 6 minutes old, so the whole namespace had just been (re)started. Every service has endpoints.\n- **Cause:** The frontend's only errors were `14 UNAVAILABLE ... ECONNREFUSED` to the `ad` service (10.96.129.134:8080). They happened early, while `ad` was still starting. The `accounting` pod only began consuming from Kafka after its `wait-for-kafka` init container finished, about 5m47s before I checked. That delay is the likely source of the latency alert. I did not check the alert rules or metrics directly.\n- **Current health:**\n  - In the last 60 to 90 seconds, `frontend` logged no errors and `frontend-proxy` logged no 5xx responses.\n  - Frontend requests are returning 200, and orders are being placed successfully.\n  - `accounting` is processing orders with no errors or warnings.\n- **Flags:** All flagd feature flags are `off`, so no fault injection is active.\n\nPlease confirm the three alerts have resolved. If they keep firing, tell me, because the alert rules may be evaluating over a window that still includes the startup period.",
    "timed_out": false,
